The release. One feature: a plain explainer of why income is asked and how it is used. It is copy on a question that already exists, so it ships as a release, not a campaign. The product owner freezes that copy on day one of intake.

The goal. More kept instalments, which is the reliable money. The file counts agreements and 60-day misses, not instalments inside an agreement, so the working unit is a kept agreement: starters × agreement rate × 60-day hold.

The audience. Variable-or-shift starters in the portal, at the income question. A sample month has 2,862 of them. They agree at 41.6%, and 22.5% of those agreements miss within 60 days, the highest miss in the worksheet, which is a 77.5% hold. That hold is also the floor in your ship rule. Two-claim and three-or-more starters stay outside this release: the worksheet describes them as needing a person, and this copy answers the income question.

The read. Intake is the first 7 sample-months, about 1,430 people per arm, about 10,010 per arm. A 2-point lift at 80% power needs about 9,600 per arm, so the test is sized. The one read is 60 days after intake closes. A 14-day peek cannot see the lift or the hold.

The call.

Ship if agreement rate is at least 2 percentage points above control at two-sided p < 0.05, and the hold stays at or above 77.5% and at or above control. Then the explainer goes to every variable-or-shift starter, and the help page, release note, and support note go out.
Iterate if agreement rate is above control, the lift is under 2 points, and the hold is intact. Rewrite the copy and run a new test. This is the call the worksheet marks as most likely.
Kill if agreement rate does not improve or falls, or the hold breaks. Remove the explainer and close the release.
At today’s volume, a full sample month that hit the ship bar with the hold still at 77.5% would be about 44 more kept agreements (1,191 agreements and 923 kept today, versus 1,248 and 967). That illustration uses the persona rates; the experiment itself compares arms.

Channels. The explainer on the question (treatment arm only during the test), then the help page and release note, then a support note in the same words. The third channel was blank; it is filled from your enablement line, local communications. Paid stays parked: the people who need the explanation are already at the question, and the worksheet sets no budget and no euro value for a kept agreement in this segment. The product owner is the only owner named, so the ship call sits with them.
